    "message": "fix(upgrade): make the release-bundle guard reachable from a test\n\n`shouldOfferCompassUpgrade` read the stamp itself, so the only thing the new\ntests could reach was `parseCompassStamp`. Deleting the\n`source === \"release\"` branch — the entire behavioural change in #376 — left\nall 728 tests green while restoring the inversion in full.\n\nTake the stamp as an argument and export the decision. `installedCompass()`\nnow returns the whole stamp instead of the version alone, which also stops\nthe function reading `compass/.version` twice per call.\n\nTests cover the inversion itself, the dist-series comparison that must still\nhappen, the repair path for a gutted bundle (which is why the 0.0.0 check\nsits ahead of the source check — reversing them is #365/#366 again), the\noffline case, and a legacy bare stamp. Both mutations now fail the suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
